Backport of ghostty-org/ghostty 33cda4dc5 "terminal: reload cell pointers
when print grows a page" (2026-08-22, fixes ghostty-org/ghostty#11261) onto
tai's pin a887df42. Only the code hunks: the commit's new tests use Zig
0.16's testing.io and don't build with the pinned Zig 0.15.

At the pin, Terminal.print and printCell keep cell pointers across calls
that can grow, and so replace, the cursor's page. Output with many
hyperlinks (OSC 8) then reads or writes freed memory: a ReleaseSafe build
crashed in Terminal.print on macOS, and the grapheme path writes through
the stale pointer in any build mode.

scripts/fetch-ghostty.sh applies this file. Drop it when the Ghostty pin
moves past 33cda4dc5.

